{"path":"/documentation/modeling/vllm/tracer","section":"documentation","title":"tracer","description":"Documentation for the nnsight Python library","toc":[{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer","label":"tracer","depth":2},{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.VLLMTracer","label":"VLLMTracer","depth":3},{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.no_barrier","label":"no_barrier","depth":3}],"segments":[{"type":"html","html":"<h2 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-module\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-module-name\">tracer</span>\n\n\n</h2>"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>A tracer whose workers can be built without running the model.</p>\n<p>The base <a title=\"            InterleavingTracer\" href=\"/documentation/intervention/tracer#nnsight.intervention.tracer.InterleavingTracer\"><code>InterleavingTracer</code></a> builds a trace's\nworkers and, in the same step, runs the forward. An async vLLM trace instead hands\nthe request to the engine and streams the outputs, so it needs the worker-building\nstep on its own, before any forward. <a title=\"            VLLMTracer\" href=\"#nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.VLLMTracer\"><code>VLLMTracer</code></a> factors that step into\n<a title=\"            prepare\" href=\"#nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.VLLMTracer.prepare\"><code>prepare</code></a>; the synchronous path (<code>execute</code>) still runs it and then the\nforward, exactly as the base does. Keeping this in the vLLM package leaves the base\ntracer untouched.</p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.VLLMTracer\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-class\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-class-name\">VLLMTracer</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"VLLMTracer(envoy: Envoy, fn: Callable | str, *args: Any, backend: Backend | None = None, **kwargs: Any)"},{"type":"html","html":"<p class=\"doc-class-bases\">\n              Bases: <code><a title=\"            InterleavingTracer (nnsight.intervention.tracer.InterleavingTracer)\" href=\"/documentation/intervention/tracer#nnsight.intervention.tracer.InterleavingTracer\">InterleavingTracer</a></code></p>\n\n\n\n        <p>An <a title=\"            InterleavingTracer\" href=\"/documentation/intervention/tracer#nnsight.intervention.tracer.InterleavingTracer\"><code>InterleavingTracer</code></a> whose worker-building is callable on its own.</p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.VLLMTracer.barrier\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">barrier</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"barrier(n: int) -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Not available here — see <a title=\"            no_barrier\" href=\"#nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.no_barrier\"><code>no_barrier</code></a>.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.VLLMTracer.prepare\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">prepare</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"prepare(code: CodeType) -> tuple"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Build the trace's workers and combined call input, without running the model.</p>\n<p>The first half of <code>execute</code>: collect the invoke workers (or the single\ndirect-input worker) onto the interleaver and assemble the batched call\ninput, then return the workers alongside it. The async backend uses this to\nget the workers to serialize and the input to submit, in place of\n<a title=\"            interleave\" href=\"/documentation/intervention/envoy#nnsight.intervention.envoy.Envoy.interleave\"><code>interleave</code></a>.</p>\n\n\n<table>\n      <thead>\n        <tr>\n          <th><span class=\"doc-section-title\">RETURNS</span></th>\n          <th><span>DESCRIPTION</span></th>\n        </tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n          <tr class=\"doc-section-item\">\n            <td>\n                <span class=\"doc-returns-annotation\">\n                    <code><span title=\"tuple\">tuple</span></code>\n                </span>\n            </td>\n            <td class=\"doc-returns-details\">\n              <div class=\"doc-md-description\">\n                <p><code>(workers, args, kwargs)</code> — the workers to read results from, and the</p>\n              </div>\n            </td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr class=\"doc-section-item\">\n            <td>\n                <span class=\"doc-returns-annotation\">\n                    <code><span title=\"tuple\">tuple</span></code>\n                </span>\n            </td>\n            <td class=\"doc-returns-details\">\n              <div class=\"doc-md-description\">\n                <p>combined <code>(args, kwargs)</code> for the model call.</p>\n              </div>\n            </td>\n          </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.VLLMTracer.execute\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">execute</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"execute(code: CodeType) -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Build the workers, run the forward interleaved, push results back.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.tracer.no_barrier\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-function\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">no_barrier</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"no_barrier(n: int) -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Refuse a barrier, which this runtime cannot hold.</p>\n<p>A barrier releases when <code>n</code> of a trace's blocks have reached it, which\nneeds them all running against one forward. Here each invoke is a separate\nvLLM request, scheduled independently and possibly in different steps\nentirely, so the blocks never coexist and the barrier would simply never\nrelease — a hang rather than an error. Say so at the call instead.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"}]}